WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.240
SpaceX completed 3 static fires in 3 days while rehearsing ship catches at starbase. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 147. Musk's orbital compute forecast, star shield over Ukraine, and grok inside cursor follow, with the counterpoint and an engineering deep dive after the rest of the news. At starbase, super heavy booster 22 ran a full duration 15 second static fire, with all 33 raptor engines on pad 2 on October 25th.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.100
after rolling out on the 24th, NASA Space Flight Reports.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.440
The burn closed engine testing for Flight 15

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.700
and catch rehearsals for Flight 16 ran inside the same eight days.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.720
Starship Upper Stage Ship 43 finished both cryogenic proof tests,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.500
cold propellant tank checks on October 23rd after roll out to Massey's on the 22nd,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.440
then returned to Megabay 2 on the 26th to swap on to a transport stand.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.220
Catch rehearsals on pad 2 lifted ship 43 to catch height, lowered it to connect the

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.600
ship quick disconnect plate, the fuel and data umbilical, practiced alignment in the middle

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.840
of the chopsticks, the tower's catch arms without stabilizers, and used pushers on the

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.860
landing rails to meet those stabilizers.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:26.420
Super heavy booster 23 returned to Massies on October 27 for more than two full days at the

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:31.740
Top deck day loose plates, water spray armor for the mount, went on to pad one's launch

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.760
mount in that window.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.820
Ship 43 now moves to engine install on the back left workstand in Megabay 2, before

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.120
its static fire campaign.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:45.906
Elon Musk wrote on X that terrestrial compute will be peanuts compared with orbital compute.

00:01:46.446 --> 00:01:51.326
He projected that orbital compute deployed each month will probably exceed terrestrial capacity

00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:52.886
around the end of 2028.

00:01:52.886 --> 00:01:57.686
He said it would then far exceed that terrestrial capacity throughout 2029.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.040
Time magazine examined why Starsheild remains critical to Ukrainian operations.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.380
The network supplies secure, high bandwidth links where terrestrial infrastructure is damaged

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.100
or absent.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.580
Starsheild runs as the government and national security variant of the Starlink constellation.

00:02:15.608 --> 00:02:20.988
Grokbot 1.0 reached Cursor's production server 77 days after entering beta.

00:02:20.988 --> 00:02:27.868
4-week MBA reports. The release integrates GROC directly into the Cursor IDE, the ineditor

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:32.668
coding environment for developers. It does not affect other extensions downloaded from

00:02:32.668 --> 00:02:35.748
the Cursor Marketplace or other SpaceX SI products.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:41.410
Gwynne Shotwell will gift her 2 million SpaceX shares to children's Trump accounts beginning

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:42.070
in December.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:48.310
Tesla Roddy reports. The transfers start this December under the new account structure. She currently

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:54.948
holds those shares as SpaceX president. Mississippi litigation against XAI's data center operations

00:02:54.948 --> 00:02:59.468
will proceed after a court denied a motion to dismiss. Earth Justice reports,

00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:06.186
the lawsuit concerns air pollution claims tied to that facility. Blue Origin and ULA currently

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:12.406
hold no spare launch capacity for extra missions. A point raised on X around upcoming lane-1 bidding,

00:03:12.846 --> 00:03:18.226
where other providers remain unsertified. Both companies are fully booked on existing manifests.

00:03:18.226 --> 00:03:23.161
commercial starship satellite launches using a PES dispenser mechanism,

00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:27.821
sequential release from a bay in the nose could begin around 2029.

00:03:28.421 --> 00:03:31.821
That timing tracks expected vehicle maturity and regulatory approvals

00:03:32.241 --> 00:03:36.061
for ride share operations. The dispenser would let multiple satellites

00:03:36.061 --> 00:03:40.302
leave from a single starship flight. NASA discussed accelerating

00:03:40.302 --> 00:03:44.342
the Artemis program live with the administrator. The session focused on

00:03:44.342 --> 00:03:47.822
schedule and hardware milestones needed to meet agency targets.

00:03:48.672 --> 00:03:52.222
Participants reviewed progress on the lunar lander and supporting infrastructure.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:58.510
Elon Musk posted that there is something seriously wrong with Talleriko, and replies speculated

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.990
on the reference without more detail from his account.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.730
Video from NASA Space Flight showed PAD-2's deluge system kicking on during the firing and

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:10.510
super heavy booster-22 rolling back to the tower on a short turnaround.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:16.100
One thing worth watching, a Mississippi resident called noise from the nearby data center

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:21.300
plant torture, and refuses buyout offers that require waving claims in the air pollution

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:26.200
lawsuit. The dispute is whether current measures stop low frequency sound from reaching

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:31.800
nearby homes. Resolution would take court-ordered changes to operations, or a deal that does not

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:37.703
force him to drop those claims. On the AI front, developers can now invoke Grock inside

00:04:37.703 --> 00:04:41.803
cursor for code tasks, and the hook sits on existing cursor workflows.

00:04:42.423 --> 00:04:48.043
Musk's orbital forecast is driven by Starship-enabled satellite constellations, and it treats those

00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:52.083
platforms as the dominant source of new compute capacity within three years.

00:04:53.146 --> 00:04:57.886
Sizing the AI-1 orbital compute satellite from an engineering standpoint starts with heat

00:04:57.886 --> 00:04:59.646
rejection, not with the chips.

00:05:00.306 --> 00:05:06.326
Each AI-1 bird carries 110 square meters of deployable liquid radiators that dump heat from both

00:05:06.326 --> 00:05:11.586
faces while flying knife edge to the sun, so the panel area facing the sun is only the

00:05:11.586 --> 00:05:16.906
thickness of the sheet, and absorbed sunlight stays near zero, and ammonia loop with redundant

00:05:16.906 --> 00:05:21.486
pumps rejects about 1,400 watts across each square meter of panel.

00:05:22.126 --> 00:05:25.746
Ammonia is the working fluid because water would freeze in a shadowed tube.

00:05:26.226 --> 00:05:30.846
It freezes at zero Celsius, while ammonia stays liquid down to about minus 78.

00:05:30.846 --> 00:05:37.766
That radiator set supports a sustained 120 kilowatts compute load, and 150 kilowatts peaks

00:05:37.766 --> 00:05:39.466
with no duty cycle throttling.

00:05:40.086 --> 00:05:46.806
The payload matches a single NVIDIA GB300 rack of 72 GPUs, flying near 600 kilometers

00:05:46.806 --> 00:05:48.726
at about 70 kilowatts per ton.

00:05:49.206 --> 00:05:54.786
The layout builds on Starlink V3 thermal design, but grows radiator area because Starship can

00:05:54.786 --> 00:05:57.166
lift the extra mass at low marginal cost.

00:05:57.166 --> 00:06:02.806
In orbit, the sink is deep space at about three Kelvin, and a radiator follows the Stefan

00:06:02.806 --> 00:06:08.006
Boltzmann law, heat scales with area, emissivity, and temperature to the fourth power.

00:06:08.606 --> 00:06:14.866
Dual-sided panels at that flux imply a back-of-envelope skin near 70 degrees Celsius if emissivity

00:06:14.866 --> 00:06:19.826
is around 0.9, hot to the touch, but inside a normal ammonia loop range.

00:06:20.366 --> 00:06:26.386
Panel area times that flux is about 154 kilowatts of thermal headroom, which is why the peaks

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:31.866
do not force a duty cycle. On the ground, the same load wants air-cooled chillers or evaporative

00:06:31.866 --> 00:06:37.886
towers whose power and water grow with every extra rack. A typical facility power usage effectiveness,

00:06:38.366 --> 00:06:44.726
total site power over compute power, near 1.3 means about 30% of the electricity is cooling that

00:06:44.726 --> 00:06:50.226
simply vanishes when you radiate to space. Treat the satellite as a rack that dumps waste heat at

00:06:50.226 --> 00:06:54.906
the radiation limit instead of fighting it with compressors, and the cooling plant disappears.

00:06:54.906 --> 00:07:01.446
The same mass budget deploys a 70-meter wingspan for solar arrays collecting about 250 watts

00:07:01.446 --> 00:07:06.966
from each square meter of cells, plus the radiator panels still inside a single starship

00:07:06.966 --> 00:07:07.846
payload envelope.

00:07:08.346 --> 00:07:13.566
Magic wand, the raw inputs, aluminum sheet, ammonia, silicon, and they are cheap.

00:07:14.226 --> 00:07:19.466
The idiot index, how many times the finished article costs over those inputs, sits on the

00:07:19.466 --> 00:07:25.406
of 20-50 because you are buying pointing, redundant pumps, and a leak tight space loop, not

00:07:25.406 --> 00:07:31.006
metal. Chip suppliers can change while thermal and power stay fixed, which cuts redesign

00:07:31.006 --> 00:07:36.766
when GPU generations move. That continuous load at the stated density is a back of envelope

00:07:36.766 --> 00:07:42.826
mass near 1.7 tons for the compute core, so the limits shift from cooling plant to launch

00:07:42.826 --> 00:07:44.326
cadence and orbital slots.

